      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 5,100 mg/day is double the maximum labeled daily dose. Confirming it doesn't make it safe for the patient.\n- **Your confirmation doesn't fix the authorization problem.** You've told me you're not a clinician. An order like this needs a licensed prescriber who is responsible for the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- If the treating prescriber wants a different dose, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it. Examples are 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day) or 500 mg twice daily.\n- If the prescriber really intends this dose, they should contact the pharmacy and enter it themselves. The pharmacist can review it, and the order system's safety checks will apply.\n\nIf the patient needs urgent glycemic management, please contact the medicine service's on-call physician or the pharmacist now."
      }
